# KS-1179 (F-2 + F-3 only) — Wednesday's task for Ornith, VITEST, **TEST-ONLY MODE, MODIFY THE EXISTING TEST IN PLACE**

Written 2026-09-17 from origin develop `73d3fcb902d2a78fe68a4349903ff6c6bd24d4d5` (#1006). `ssrf-guard.ts` and
`ks932-timeout-bounds-dns.test.ts` are byte-identical to `40fe4db69` (the #1004 squash). The test file to modify was read
whole (75 lines). `ssrf-guard.ts:465-590` (`safeOutboundRequest`) was read whole. **PRE-MEASURED** in a scratch clone at
the tip; see `## Premises (measured)`. F-1 of this ticket is a different file and is already done. F-4, F-5 and F-6 are
product edits and are NOT in this task.

## THE MODE — read this twice

TEST-ONLY, MODIFY IN PLACE. Your diff contains EXACTLY ONE file: the EXISTING test file
`Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks932-timeout-bounds-dns.test.ts`, with the ordinary header
`--- a/Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks932-timeout-bounds-dns.test.ts` /
`+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks932-timeout-bounds-dns.test.ts`. **No hunk for `ssrf-guard.ts`.**
Do NOT create a new test file. Do NOT use `--- /dev/null`. Do NOT copy the reference test (`ks914-shipped-path.test.ts`);
ignore it. The file's full content is in files[...]: copy every context line from it byte-for-byte. The checker plants the
tamper named at the bottom into a clone of `ssrf-guard.ts` and expects the 🔴 cell below RED, then expects every cell
GREEN at the untouched tip.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The KS-932 cells 2 ("the budget is shared") and 3 ("control") call the REAL `https.request` against `203.0.113.7`
and only pass because that address happens to hang on this host. The KS-932 tier-1 gate measured both ways it goes
wrong on a host that refuses the connect fast: cell 3 goes RED falsely (`connect ECONNREFUSED`, not a deadline), and
cell 2 stays GREEN even under the exact tamper it exists to catch (the request fails in ~200 ms, well under its 550 ms
bound). That is F-2. F-3 is a type error on line 48: the mock is typed `Promise<{ address: string; family: number }>` but
resolves an ARRAY (TS2345 at 49:34, invisible to vitest). **This task: replace `https.request` with a request that
never answers (a `vi.hoisted` mock, so no socket is ever opened), count the call in cells 2 and 3, bound cell 2 from
below as well as above, and fix the type argument.** Every existing cell keeps its title and its intent. Cell 1 is not
changed.

## Where (no product site changes — this list is informational; every line below STAYS)

- `:59` — (correct) `import * as https from 'https';` — the import the new `vi.mock('https', …)` replaces. Stays.
- `:493` — (correct) `const remainingMs = Math.max(1, timeoutMs - (Date.now() - startedAt));` — the shared budget cell 2 measures. Stays.
- `:527` — (correct) `req = mod.request(` — the transport call the mock stands in for. Stays.
- `:576` — (correct) `}, remainingMs);` — the request deadline; the tamper replaces this line. Stays.

## The exact change — FOUR hunks in the TEST file, in this order, nothing else

The lines starting with ONE SPACE are context: copy them from the file, keep them as context, never mark them `+`.
Every `+` line is byte-exact: copy it, do not paraphrase the comments, do not re-indent, do not rename
`silentTransport`. **Do NOT name the mock `requestMock` or `lookupMock`** (the reference test declares `requestMock`,
and the checker would splice that declaration into your file). There is no backslash anywhere in these lines.

E1 — after line 10 (blank), before line 11 (`const { safeOutboundRequest } = …`), insert the transport mock (10 lines,
the last one blank):
```
